title: API errors lose the HTTP status and network failures look like API errors
updated: 2026-10-20T04:02:50Z
---

`lib/WWW/VastAI/Role/HTTP.pm` (`_parse_response`): on a non-2xx the croak is `"Vast.ai API error: $message"`, where `$message` is `msg`/`message`/`error` of the body, or the raw body, or the bare status number. Method and path are passed in but only used for the success log line.

Consequences: a caller cannot tell a 404 (instance gone) from a 429 (rate limit, where Vast.ai expects a back-off) or a 401 without parsing free text; an HTML error page from the CDN is dumped whole into the message; a connection failure (LWP's internal 500 with a text body) reads `Vast.ai API error: Can't connect to ...`. In addition `decode_json($content)` runs before the status check without `eval`, so a truncated or non-JSON body starting with `{` dies with a JSON::XS message, and `LWPIO::call` hands over `decoded_content` (characters for `text/*`), on which `decode_json` dies with `Wide character` as soon as the body has non-ASCII text.

Done when: the error carries status, method and path (an exception object that stringifies to the current text keeps `$@ =~` matching working), the body is truncated in the message, network failures are distinguishable, JSON decoding is guarded and done on bytes (`$response->content` after `decoded_content( charset => 'none' )`).

