2026-10-20 03:58 Commit 437f587 on branch k3-k5 (worktree .claude/worktrees/k3-k5).

Decision: the failure is reported as a new exception object WWW::VastAI::Error (Moo, like the house pattern of WWW::PayPal::Error / WWW::iDRAC::Error). It stringifies to 'Vast.ai API error: <message> (status 404, GET /instances/123/)', so the old prefix and the API message stay contiguous and $@ =~ /Vast.ai API error: .../ keeps matching, while status, method and path are appended in parentheses. A transport failure gets the distinct prefix 'Vast.ai connection error:' and the flag is_network, set in LWPIO from LWP's 'Client-Warning: Internal response' marker, so the HTTP role stays free of LWP details.

Body: only a body-derived text is truncated (200 characters); the API's own msg/message/error field is kept unchanged, the bare status stays the fallback. The JSON parsing is guarded by an eval and a body that looks like JSON but does not parse is reported as 'unparseable response body: ...' instead of dying with a JSON parser message. The body is decoded from bytes (decoded_content(charset => 'none') resp. $response->content), so a non-ASCII answer no longer breaks the JSON decoding.

Tests: t/errors.t (7 subtests) was red against the pre-k5 lib (7/7, behavioral, no 'Can't locate'); the byte contract is pinned by t/http-io.t.

